-- Synthetic data for the T14 migration rehearsal, loaded on top of
-- fixtures/source-schema.sql (a Supabase-shaped database). Not real data.
--
-- Every bcrypt hash below was generated with bcryptjs 3.0.3 (cost 10) from the
-- test password `vipe-rehearsal-2026`, with the `$2b$` prefix written as
-- `$2a$`, the prefix GoTrue stores (same algorithm; bcryptjs verifies both).
--
-- Cases the rehearsal checks (packages/db/migration-from-supabase/rehearse.sh):
--   * admin.a@example.test     bcrypt user used for the login smoke (re-hash to argon2id)
--   * cocina.b@example.test    NULL encrypted_password -> imported inactive, reported
--   * invitado.a@example.test  empty encrypted_password -> imported inactive, reported
--   * borrado.b@example.test   soft-deleted (deleted_at) -> user skipped, profile kept without login, reported
--   * vetado.a@example.test    banned_until in the future -> imported inactive, reported
--   * restaurant A has two open cash registers: the older one (R1) has the latest
--     activity and stays open; R2 is closed and recorded by the import
--   * restaurant A counters are stale (sku_raw = 1 while MP-0002 exists,
--     purchase_order = 1 while PO 2 exists); restaurant B has no counter rows
--   * dishes.image_url: Supabase public URLs (one object shared by both
--     restaurants, one with a folder and a space), a placeholder, NULL, a URL to
--     a missing object, an SVG (refused by the copy, as the API refuses SVG
--     uploads), and an object no dish references
--
-- Loaded with session_replication_role = replica, so the guard and numbering
-- triggers of the source schema do not rewrite the synthetic rows; every
-- reference is consistent by construction.
SET session_replication_role = replica;

